<PageShell title="Curriculum Development Accomplishments">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      One of my primary accomplishments during this review period has been establishing a more systematic
      approach to online Biology course development.
    </p>
    <p>
      The redesigned Biology course model emphasizes alignment with departmental learning outcomes,
      consistent organization, purposeful assessments, adaptive learning, meaningful laboratory
      experiences, multiple instructional modalities, and reduced reliance on assignments that can be
      completed through simple copying or generic AI-generated responses.
    </p>
    <p>
      As the Biology course development process has progressed, my responsibilities have expanded beyond
      Biology. I have begun supporting the redesign of HSI 212, HHP 345, and HHP 209 after discussing the
      Biology course design model with colleagues in those areas.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also identified a gap in the online Biology curriculum: although Doane offers on-ground Biology
      courses, an online Ecology course was not available. I raised this need with the Biology Chair, and
      we subsequently developed a modern, comprehensive and academically rigorous online Ecology course.
    </p>
    <p>
      Looking ahead, I will to continue evaluating the online course portfolio to identify additional
      opportunities for growth for Doane University. I have co-developed a microcredential proposal for a
      Post-Baccalaureate Pre-Health Certificate, which represents a potential future avenue for serving
      students who need structured preparation for health-professional programs. This certificate will
      provide additional services for students who want to enter the medical field, such as academic
      advising, letters of recommendation and structured courses to meet prerequisites for their
      professional programs.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageShell>
